FreeScout on FenrirOS
=====================

Code in /usr/share/freescout (web root: public/). Its .env is
/etc/freescout/env; storage/, Modules/ and bootstrap/cache live in
/var/lib/freescout (links from the code directory). PHP runs as _php.

1. Create a MariaDB database and user for FreeScout.
2. cp /usr/share/freescout/.env.example /etc/freescout/env, chown _php it,
   and set APP_URL and the database (or let the web installer fill it).
3. nginx: /usr/share/doc/freescout/nginx-freescout.conf; enable php-fpm and
   nginx, then open https://<host>/install and follow the installer.
4. Enable crond (dinitctl enable crond): /etc/cron.d/freescout runs the
   scheduler (mail fetching and queues).
